    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d655">

                <pb facs="0959" n="1467" sameAs="frus:frus1948v05p2/pg1467"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BB Palestine/10–1148: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Presidents Special Counsel</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Clifford</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting
                        Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lovett</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Aboard <placeName type="venue">Presidential
                                Special</placeName> Train</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1948-10-11T23:30:00">October 11, 1948—11:30
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p> Black 93. I have your White 174.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d655-f1"/> Have discussed
                    the matter with the President and he directs me to inform you that your existing
                    instructions are cancelled.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d655-f2"/> If you are asked
                    questions on Wednesday<anchor n="3" xml:id="d655-f3"/> you are to make no
                    comment.</p>
                <p>We note with great interest the plan of the Secretary to discuss alternative
                    language on arrival in Paris. We feel it would be most helpful if he would
                    include Ben Cohen<anchor n="4" xml:id="d655-f4"/> in such discussion because of
                    the latter’s familiarity with our problems here.<anchor n="5" xml:id="d655-f5"/>
                </p>
                <p>Will appreciate your forwarding to us as soon as possible any new language. If
                    you prefer we can always be reached by telephone.</p>
                <p>Best regards,</p>
                <closer>[<signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Clark Clifford</hi>
                    </signed>]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d655-f1" n="1" xml:id="d655-f1-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Supra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d655-f2" n="2" xml:id="d655-f2-content">
                <p>The expression “existing instructions” possibly refers to Presidential
                    authorization for Mr. Lovett to use the statement.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d655-f3" n="3" xml:id="d655-f3-content">
                <p>October 13, the date of Mr. Lovett’s press conference.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d655-f4" n="4" xml:id="d655-f4-content">
                <p>Benjamin V. Cohen, Alternative Representative in the United States Delegation at
                    the first part of the Third Session of the General Assembly at Paris.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d655-f5" n="5" xml:id="d655-f5-content">
                <p>Acting Secretary Lovett quoted this paragraph in part to Secretary Marshall in
                    telegram Telmar 63, October 12, 1 p. m., to Paris (501.BB
                    Palestine/10–1248).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
